# Maewyn Ashvale, companion quest, part one: the raven comes back thin.
#
# CANON (maewyn.agd): a stone cottage in a hollow, herb beds, four to six
# hives, two ravens, THIRTY YEARS of keeping it. She is alone there - "the
# hills talk," and then, quieter, "they don't answer." When she agreed to
# ride she looked at the whole of it and said "the hills can hold it a
# while," and pulled the door shut without locking it.
#
# There is no circle and no order and nobody waiting. That is the point. The
# grove has no keeper because the keeper is here, and a while has turned out
# to have a length.
#
# VOICE: terse. Her lines run short; the pauses and the bird do the talking.
#
# {PLAYER} is whoever is nearest when the raven lands.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_MaewynRaven

== start ==
The second raven comes in low and lands badly.

It is thin. Maewyn takes it onto her wrist and goes through it without a word: keel, wing, feet, eyes. Corvus watches from her shoulder and does not make a sound, which from him is alarming.

Then she opens its beak and takes out what it has carried the whole way.

* [Wait.] -> what
* "What is that?" -> what

== what ==
It is a sprig of something grey and dry, gone to seed and past it.

She turns it over twice.

"Sagewort. From the third bed." A pause. "It flowers in spring. It should not have seed on it in any year I am there."

* "Meaning?" -> meaning
* [Say nothing.] -> meaning

== meaning ==
"Meaning nobody cut it. Meaning nobody has cut anything since I left."

She puts the bird on her knee. It stays there, which it has never done either.

"He has been going back. Both of them have. Every few weeks, all this time, to look at a house with nobody in it." A pause. "This one stopped eating properly to bring me a weed."

* "How long since you were there?" -> howlong
* "You said the hills could hold it." -> hold

== howlong ==
She works it out. It takes her a moment, and the moment is the answer.

"Too long, apparently."

* "You said the hills could hold it." -> hold

== hold ==
"I did." Flat. "A while. I have been saying a while since the day I shut that door, and eventually a while turns into a long while."

She looks at the sprig.

"Thirty years I kept those beds. Hives, birds, the whole hollow. It does not keep itself. That was rather the arrangement."

* "Then we go back." -> back
* "It is a garden, Maewyn." -> garden

== garden ==
The look she gives you is not angry.

"It is nine kinds of things that grow nowhere else in this valley. It is hives that will swarm and die without a hand on them. It is the only place within sixty miles where a trained hand can get what it needs to keep a person alive."

A pause.

"And a house. Yes. It is a garden."

* "Then we go back." -> back

== back ==
"Aye."

She does not thank you. She does not need to.

"Two days off the road. Bring the shovel."

* "Two days." -> end
    do flag(TSC_MaewynGroveAsked); give_quest(TSC_Maewyn_ThirtyYears); affinity(+5)
